.TH CSTRING_RESET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_reset \- clear all characters and shrink capacity to minimum
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

void cstring_reset(cstr s);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Sets the length to zero and then tries to shrink the buffer back to the
minimum capacity of 16 bytes. When that reallocation fails, the capacity
stays the same; the length always becomes zero in both cases.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s   String to reset
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_set (3),
.BR cstring_is_empty (3)
